        "original_id": "f110593f-393b-5e7a-8760-338eeb96ce2c",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Erlend Øye\n- Organizations: Kings of Convenience, Belle and Sebastian, Hjálmar, The Whitest Boy Alive\n- Places: Bergen, Norway, Glasgow, Scotland, Reykjavík, Iceland, Seoul\n- Products: Legao, “Garota”\n- Concepts: indie folk-pop duo, Scottish band, solo album, reggae group\n\nFacts:\n- Kings of Convenience is an indie folk-pop duo from Bergen, Norway.\n- Belle and Sebastian is a Scottish band that was formed in Glasgow in January 1996.\n- Legao is the second solo album by Erlend Øye, who is a singer in Kings of Convenience and The Whitest Boy Alive.\n- Erlend Øye recorded Legao in Reykjavík with Hjálmar, a reggae group from Iceland.\n- The single “Garota” anticipated Legao, and its videoclip was shot in Seoul.",
